== what is wrong with a lesson is said by line ==
  line 2: @solution is never closed with ' @end
  line 1: exercise a has no @check, so nothing can say whether it is done
  --
  line 1: @end with nothing open
  --
  line 3: a @starter line must be commented out (it is the student's code, not the instructor's)
  --
  line 3: a check line cannot end in a comment -- put the comment on its own line
  line 2: this @check has no `print <expression>` line to check
  --
  line 2: this @check has no `print <expression>` line to check
  --
  line 5: exercise a is already defined at line 1
  --
  line 1: an exercise id is lower-case letters, digits, - and _ (got "Mean!")
  --
  line 4: @solution inside an open @check (line 2) -- close it with ' @end first
  --
  line 1: @solution before any @exercise
  line 2: @end with nothing open
  --
  line 2: @check takes nothing or `private` (got "public")
  line 5: @answer is not a lesson marker (exercise, solution, starter, check, end, hint, tutor)
  --
  line 1: exercise a has no @check, so nothing can say whether it is done
  --
  line 2: exercise a has a @starter but no @solution for it to replace
  --
