== what the notes say when the lesson itself is wrong ==
  a wrong solution, and a starter that is the answer:
  lesson-checked: checked 3 exercise(s): the solutions pass 1 of 3, but 1 already pass(es) in the student edition — see the notes under each exercise
  lesson-average: **Solution fails:** the checks on lines 47, 48, 51 fail. The student edition fails 2 of its 2 public check(s), as it should until the student does the exercise.
  lesson-middle: **Solution passes** its 3 check(s). **The starter already passes** every public check, so the exercise gives itself away.
  lesson-spread: **Solution fails:** the checks on lines 107, 110 fail. The student edition fails 1 of its 1 public check(s), as it should until the student does the exercise.
  a starter that divides by zero -- and the summary at the end calls it, so every run of the edition stops there:
  lesson-checked: checked 3 exercise(s): the solutions pass 3 of 3, and none is already done in the student edition
  lesson-average: **Solution passes** its 3 check(s). **The student edition does not run**, at its line 64: division by zero
  lesson-middle: **Solution passes** its 3 check(s). **The student edition does not run**, at its line 64: division by zero
  lesson-spread: **Solution passes** its 2 check(s). **The student edition does not run**, at its line 64: division by zero
